WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.940
Hello everyone.

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:02.880
Welcome to the Langfocus channel

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.580
and my name is Paul.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:05.900
As you probably know.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:07.720
(Nope, never heard of you!)

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.220
In this video I want to talk about something that people often ask me about

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.000
but then I don't usually talk about in videos...

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.720
...and that's how I study languages.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:21.440
I don't usually talk about it because I don't want to portray Langfocus as a polyglot channel.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.820
And whenever i talk about the way I learn

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.320
some people blow it out of proportion and they they think

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.160
that I must be some language learning master  or guru which I'm not.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.760
and also 'cause I'm so busy making videos all the time these days

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.220
I don't to give the people false impression that I spend all day studying languages

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:44.220
and reviewing ones that I've studied in the past.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:48.220
But with that said, I do study usually during my commute,

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.080
which is probably about an hour of uninterrupted time if I've calculated.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.940
at the moment I'm  focussing on in Indonesian,

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:56.940
I studied it a long time ago, but this year I've decided to review it.

